"Burflax" <Burflax@aol.com> wrote:

>Is it patch -p0 --dry-run < Filename.diff or what?

It depends on the patch.

For example, using Jukka Lahtinen's combined diff:

	phlucas@hier /dose/nethacks/pt
	$ patch -p0 < nh343jl.diff
	patching file README.nh343jl
	patching file dat/opthelp
	patching file dat/wizhelp
	patching file doc/Guidebook.mn
	patching file doc/Guidebook.tex
	...

The argument to -p is the depth of directories to skip as prefixed.

